            <h1>What are the roles of automated mold lubrication and coolin=
g equipment in precision die forging production?</h1>
            <div class=3D"time"><i class=3D"iconfont icon-rili"></i> 2026-0=
1-29</div>
            <p>AYANK FORGING has implemented intelligent upgrades in automa=
ted mold lubrication and cooling equipment. It can achieve data linkage wit=
h forging equipment, automatically spray release agent in sync with the for=
ging cycle, and allows adjustments to spray volume, spray time, atomization=
 effect, spray position, and cycle time. The equipment is easy to install, =
convenient to use, safe, and efficient.</p>
<p><img src=3D"https://www.ayankforging.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/01/Auto=
mated-Mold-Lubrication-and-Cooling-Equipment.jpg" alt=3D"" data-src=3D"/wp-=
content/uploads/2026/01/Automated-Mold-Lubrication-and-Cooling-Equipment.jp=
g" decoding=3D"async" class=3D" lazyloaded" data-eio-rwidth=3D"1440" data-e=
io-rheight=3D"657"></p>
<p>Impact of Traditional Spraying Methods on the Forging Industry</p>
<p><iframe width=3D"400" height=3D"224" src=3D"cid:frame-5C35DAC29406D045C5=
3E433334CB6CED@mhtml.blink" allowfullscreen=3D"allowfullscreen"></iframe></=
p>
<p>Currently, most forging production relies on manual operation of simple =
spraying devices to apply release agent. Workers in the high-temperature, h=
igh-pressure forging environment are susceptible to mechanical injuries, bu=
rns, scalds, heat radiation, as well as hazards from fumes, dust, and noise=
. There have also been cases of explosions involving pressure vessels stori=
ng release agent in simple spraying equipment due to their proximity to hea=
t sources.</p>
<p>Impact of Automated Lubrication and Cooling Equipment on the Forging Ind=
ustry</p>
<p>Automated mold lubrication and cooling equipment can reduce or eliminate=
 manual operation links, decreasing worker workload. It minimizes the need =
for workers to approach forging equipment and hot forgings, avoiding areas =
with fumes and potential splash zones from the workpiece surface, thereby p=
rotecting workers from accidental injuries during operation. AYANK FORGING'=
s newly developed release agent spraying equipment=E2=80=94the automated mo=
ld lubrication and cooling system=E2=80=94has fully considered safety perfo=
rmance. It features structural upgrades to avoid safety risks and incorpora=
tes intelligent enhancements. It can achieve data linkage with forging equi=
pment, automatically spray release agent in sync with the forging cycle, an=
d allows adjustments to spray volume, spray time, atomization effect, spray=
 position, and cycle time. The equipment is easy to install, convenient to =
use, safe, and efficient.</p>
<p>AYANK FORGING Automated Mold Lubrication and Cooling Equipment</p>
<p>The automated mold lubrication and cooling equipment developed and produ=
ced by AYANK FORGING adopts a split structure, consisting of three main par=
ts: the workstation, the controller, and the fixed/retractable spray head.<=
/p>
<p><strong>Workstation Function:</strong>=E2=80=8B Stores the release agent=
 and continuously stirs it; stores cleaning fluid; features a one-click cle=
aning function to clean the release agent channels when not in use.</p>
<p><strong>Controller:</strong>=E2=80=8B Equipped with a touchscreen for ea=
sy adjustment of parameters such as spray time, spray direction, spray posi=
tion, system pressure, and spray cycle.</p>
<p><strong>Fixed/Retractable Spray Head:</strong>=E2=80=8B The direct spray=
ing interface.</p>
<p><strong>Fixed Spray Head</strong></p>
<p><iframe width=3D"400" height=3D"224" src=3D"cid:frame-76C890A04929374237=
4263E4E9B98DD2@mhtml.blink" allowfullscreen=3D"allowfullscreen"></iframe></=
p>
<p><strong>Retractable Spray Head</strong></p>
<p><iframe width=3D"400" height=3D"224" src=3D"cid:frame-9B62A5BF73FA53F93D=
6F911211654051@mhtml.blink" allowfullscreen=3D"allowfullscreen"></iframe></=
p>
<p>AYANK FORGING's automated mold lubrication and cooling equipment utilize=
s intelligent control. The data control system is integrated via aviation c=
onnectors for plug-and-play connection with forging equipment, enabling dat=
a coordination with the workstation. It automatically sprays release agent =
in sync with the forging cycle, improving forging efficiency.</p>
<p>The equipment also features a one-click cleaning function, allowing the =
spray pipeline to be cleaned after work, preventing release agent sedimenta=
tion and clogging in the spray tubes, thereby extending the equipment's ser=
vice life.</p>
<p>About AYANK FORGING</p>
<p>AYANK FORGING is an innovative technology company focused on forging equ=
ipment design, forging production line modification, design and installatio=
n of automated precision forging production lines, and forging technology c=
onsulting. The company integrates R&amp;D, design, service, and installatio=
n/commissioning, providing the following forging-related services: forging =
process design, technical support and services, design of automated forging=
 production lines (including layout and process design), production and ins=
tallation/commissioning of equipment for automated forging lines, forging e=
quipment and various auxiliary equipment required for automated production =
lines, and modification of automated equipment and production lines. Its se=
rvices cover multiple industry sectors including automotive parts, petroleu=
m, aviation, aerospace, rigging and tools, and power hardware.</p>
